# grok CLI integration

Contract: `GROKBUILD_ACP_CLIENT_AIM.md`. GrokBuild is a thin ACP client.

## Services

- `GrokProcess` — spawns `grok agent … stdio`, parses ACP into `AcpEvent`s. Handshake and prompt failures name the pending ACP method (`ACP initialize timed out.`, `ACP session/prompt failed.`). An empty stdout `FileHandle` fire while the child is still running is not ACP close.
- `GrokCLIService` — bounded one-shot CLI commands (`run`, session list, `--version`, structured MCP/extension management, `formatVersionOutput`).
- `ChatStore` — bridges UI to `GrokProcess`, session resume IDs, permission settings.
- `UpdateChecker` — grok CLI via `grok update --check --json`. The GrokBuild app-release feed stays off on this personal line. Install with `make ship`.

## After changing these services

Run `make test` and update `ARCHITECTURE.md`, `README.md` (if user-visible), and this rule or `grokbuild-grok-cli` skill when integration contracts change.

## Turn, permission, and reload boundaries

- `turn_completed` must cross `AcpEvent.turnCompleted`; `ChatStore` flushes/reconciles, then acknowledges it. Never resume prompt completion from the parser side channel.
- User Stop is a distinct local terminal outcome, never a fabricated backend completion or generic failure. Capture the stopped tab/backend/process-generation identity before teardown; resume only after an exact continuity receipt re-verifies that identity, otherwise create a fresh ledgered run and state that next action.
- Permission UI and automatic responses use `GrokProcess.launchReceipt`, not mutable `@AppStorage`. GrokBuild answers ACP only; it never executes an approved edit/tool client-side.
- Question, permission, and plan cards are authoritative ACP requests keyed by backend session plus JSON-RPC request id. Tool-call ids never become reply ids. Answer the pending request once and continue the same turn; never create `[Plan approved]` or other chat-shaped response prompts.
- Runtime reloads resume `ChatStore.durableGrokSessionID`. A stale load reconciles the old exact history file before persisting an explicit recovery fork.

## CLI location

`GrokCLIService.locateGrokCLI()` and `GrokProcess` share the same search paths (`~/.grok/bin/grok`, Homebrew, `PATH`, `GROK_CLI_PATH`).

## Version display

Strip `grok ` prefix and `(hash)` from `grok --version` via `GrokCLIService.formatVersionOutput`.

## MCP and compatibility schema

- Serialize MCP edits from `GrokMCPServerDraft`; never shell-split user text. Preserve ordered stdio arguments after `--`, repeated environment/header options, explicit user/project scope, and the selected project `cwd`.
- The installed 0.2.118 CLI stores MCP environment/header values literally. Require the UI disclosure acknowledgment, keep only secret names in view-model state, and redact arguments, targets, output, and errors.
- Decode current compatibility from `externalCompat.cells` and fail closed when that key exists with a malformed shape. Codex currently exposes sessions only; never synthesize capability parity.
- One-shot extension work must use `BoundedProcess`, respect task cancellation, keep row-local receipts, and retain a previous successful inventory as stale when refresh fails.

## Do not

- Shell out with raw `Process` elsewhere — use `GrokCLIService` or `GrokProcess`.
- Reconstruct MCP commands from one text field or persist returned secret values in Settings state.
- Cache CLI version indefinitely in UI; refresh when About opens or on explicit update checks.
